# chora_test's manifest (#963).
#
# It holds nothing itself: it finds the network card through the HAL, asks
# the kernel whether the card is claimed, and starts chora on it twice.
#
# 🔑 What it MAY HAND ON is the whole of it.  A chora it starts asks for any
# PCI class, and exec_load() cuts that to this line (#743): the network
# class, with DMA, registers and the interrupt.  So both choras hold the
# card's class and no other, and the second is refused by the claim the
# first holds, not by a capability it lacks.

name chora_test
delegatable 5 0x020000 0x7
